title: 'skg-export-some-to-org : exporting to org'
pid: d305ce68-3989-42b9-8ae6-0fa431300307
body: |2-
  :PROPERTIES:
  :CUSTOM_ID: export-org
  :END:
  Exports Skg data to plain =.org= files, so the data can be read
  (and navigated on GitHub) without running Skg. No keybinding.
  It ignores the connection's skgrepo restriction: what it exports is
  decided by the most private skgrepo it asks for, below, whatever
  'skg-restrict-repo-set' (C-c v l) chose.

  It asks two things:
  - the most private owned skgrepo to include. The export includes
    that skgrepo, every owned skgrepo more public than it, and every
    foreign skgrepo.
    The default, the most private owned skgrepo (shown with
    " (no restriction)"), includes every skgrepo, with a warning
    that private notes will be exported.
  - which directory to write to (default =org-exports=). This path
    is interpreted *by the server*, relative to the project root the
    server runs from. Because the server may run inside a Docker
    container whose filesystem differs from the host Emacs runs on,
    this prompt has no tab completion. An absolute path is used
    as-is.
    Existing files in the output dir are overwritten in place; other
    files there are left untouched.
    A body line Org would read as a headline (such as a Markdown
    =* item=) is indented two spaces, making it a list item, or inside a
    =#+begin_= block is escaped with a comma, as Org itself does.
    Each exported file begins with comment lines naming the ID of the node
    it was generated from, and warning that edits made directly to the
    file will be clobbered by the next export.
contains:
- 238439fd-eed9-4a93-9671-f4fc5f71a4df
